sed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reword the Windows AC so it requires the job log to show both test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8[subprocess-run] and [process-group] as PASSED, citing the run id and job id.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.5375,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'does not list the stdin test cases named in the criterion above among its failures'","instrument='gh run view --job <id> --log'"],"finding":"The Windows acceptance criterion is satisfied by absence: the stdin cases 'not listed among its failures'. That also holds if the job aborts before collection, if the module is not collected on Windows, or if the cases are deselected. So it does not show that the fixed test actually ran and passed on Windows.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd967766e6cdb39ba","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria — '[non-codebase] ... a sweep (windows) job on main after the merge does not list the stdin test cases ... among its failures'","norm_id":"n60e8ed6a238f3dfe","priority":0.4125,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["The Windows sweep errors at setup or collection after the merge. No failures list contains the stdin cases, the AC reads as met, and the fix is unverified on the only platform where the bug occurs."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"On the Windows CI runner, a sweep (windows) job on main after the merge shows tests/unit/test_git_ssh_output_encoding.py::test_run_git_encodes_str_stdin_as_utf8[subprocess-run] and [process-group] as PASSED in its log. Evidence: run id and job id in a ticket comment.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.75,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na"