ompound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Uncheck any AC not yet evidenced, especially the [non-codebase] Windows AC, until its run and job ids are posted in a ticket comment.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E1","COH","E6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.701,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"- [x] [non-codebase] On the Windows CI runner, a `sweep (windows)` job on main after the merge does not list the stdin test cases ... Evidence: run id and job id in a ticket comment.\"","Testing: \"A `sweep (windows)` run on main after the merge shows neither stdin case in its failures.\" (future tense; no ids cited)"],"finding":"All three acceptance criteria are already checked [x], including the [non-codebase] Windows sweep criterion, but the plan records no run id or job id. The Testing section also still describes the Windows run as future work ('A sweep (windows) run on main after the merge shows...').","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f7fc7296fcca682e2","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (all three [x] boxes) vs Testing section","norm_id":"n368ca8d0afba9c43","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or completion gate reads the ticked boxes as done and closes the ticket before the Windows run has happened or been attested."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Reset the ACs to [ ]. Tick the Windows AC only after posting 'run <id>, job <id>' in a ticket comment.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a short check to the plan: list run_git callers that pass str stdin and state whether any depend on LF-exact bytes; if any do, file a follow-up ticket, otherwise record that none do.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["T2","E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"The test's expectation is wrong; the encoding under test (UTF-8) is correct.\"","\"the newline translation, which is platform behaviour of text mode and not this test's concern\"","\"No product code changes\""],"finding":"The plan asserts without checking that the LF→CRLF translation is 'platform behaviour of text mode and not this test's concern'. But run_git is product code. Any production caller that passes str stdin and depends on byte-exact LF content (e.g. git hash-object, apply, commit-tree or similar) would silently get CRLF on Windows. The plan neither audits those callers nor records the behavior as a known limitation or follow-up.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f998b6a828c961e64","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem ('The test's expectation is wrong') and Approach","norm_id":"n4ecc40ec5af0fdcf","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A production path pipes LF-terminated str content into git via run_git on Windows and stores CRLF-altered blobs or commit messages, with no test catching it once the test drops the newline."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"insufficient","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in the plan whether any run_git caller passes multi-line str stdin whose bytes git stores or applies verbatim. Either justify why CRLF translation is harmless for each one, or scope a product fix (e.g. newline='' / bytes stdin) instead of only dropping the newline from the test.","cohort":["E3","E5","F4","G5","T6","necessity","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.net-mechanism","project.portability"],"criteria":["E3"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'On Windows, text-mode subprocess stdin translates \\n into \\r\\n ... so git hashes café ✓\\r\\n.'","'That isolates the property under test (the codec) from the newline translation, which is platform behaviour of text mode and not this test's concern.'","Absence: the plan names no survey of run_git callers that pass input_data, and gives no rationale for why CRLF-translated stdin is harmless for them."],"finding":"The plan declares that only the test's expectation is wrong and that 'No product code changes' are needed. It never considers whether run_git's production stdin callers depend on byte-exact LF stdin on Windows. Text-mode LF→CRLF translation of data piped to git could corrupt stdin used as content (e.g. hash-object or patch input). If any such caller exists, the failing test caught a real product defect, and stripping the newline hides it rather than fixing it.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fe396cc1ebd4e0db7","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Context / Problem — 'The test's expectation is wrong; the encoding under test (UTF-8) is correct.' and Approach — 'No product code changes'","norm_id":"n004b09691199c043","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A Windows user of a rebar path that pipes multi-line content through run_git (str stdin) gets CRLF-altered bytes stored or applied by git. The newly portable test no longer detects this."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.3333,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"na","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"insufficient","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"insufficient","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":